      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "What happens to the 64 older contracts: rewrite, archive, or leave?",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-q-older-contracts"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "answered",
        "body": "They use retired vocabulary (manifest, legend, dictionary, the old class bindings) and are unlisted now. Rewriting all of them is a project of its own and most are skill and bridge material nobody cites. Archiving means moving them under contracts/archive and updating the 48 files that cite the old addresses and the retired-vocabulary test's list. Leaving them costs nothing and is the current state. My lean: leave them, rewrite the ones a law document or the tutorial turns out to need.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793211204335,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "answeredAt": "2026-10-28T19:09:12.760Z",
        "answer": "Retire the skill and manifest-era contracts (73 files: everything under skills/, boundary, core protocols, onboarding, and the manifest, legend, dictionary, migration and validation graphs). They stay on disk as unrendered reference and are never deleted or listed. The rest are rebuilt as work needs them, and the thirteen listed ones are reviewed first, because they were only converted to the new words, not checked.",
        "resolution": "Michael, 2026-10-28"
      }
    },
