        "title": "Custom roots: the Weekend Reading Group example and the Declaration Template",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "library-made-current",
          "nodeId": "library-made-current-custom-roots"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "todo",
        "body": "A custom root (a root drawn through a node class of its own) has not been discussed since the vocabulary change, and Michael found the example wrong. What exists: the example graph \"Weekend Reading Group\" (mikemartinez1974/public/templates/declaration-template/example/root.node, 7 nodes, personal library, not canon) whose root carries classRef custom-declaration; the Declaration Template in canon (library/templates/declaration-template, a 25-node page with its class \"Custom Declaration\": Editor, Detail and Summary faces, no Icon); a second copy under templates/declaration-template-trial; and the Root primitive page, whose Examples section points at the example and whose Where-this-lives names tests/declarationTemplate.test.js and declarationDefaults.test.js. The names are still the old ones (Declaration Template, Custom Declaration). Things to decide at the hearing: does a root need a class at all, or is a custom root just faces and ground; if it stays, rename to Root Template and Custom Root; what the example should show; whether the example moves to canon; what happens to the trial copy; and what the Root primitive says about it. Nothing is changed until then.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1793217661116,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
